(7506107, 1196590, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that contributes well to the open challenge<br/> <br/>Its great idea Asmundur and very well executed. Have the band seen it? I think they should be delighted with it, I can see it as a cover on their next album. I like it because unlike a straight shot of a band it makes you look and identify more closely with the individuals, I feel the shared passion in a more individual way than I would if it were a normal shot. I like your studio set up too the brick wall and its hangings add to the end result. A great image well done.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An interesting image that contributes well to the open challenge Its great idea Asmundur and very well executed. Have the band seen it? I think they should be delighted with it, I can see it as a cover on their next album. I like it because unlike a straight shot of a band it makes you look and identify more closely with the individuals, I feel the shared passion in a more individual way than I would if it were a normal shot. I like your studio set up too the brick wall and its hangings add to the end result. A great image well done.', '2017-03-22 15:34:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(7506112, 1196898, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that contributes well to the open challenge<br/> <br/>Welcome to DPC Christopher! As a dog lover your image is bound to appeal to me, however, the timing could be better. Its true what they say, the eyes are the gateway to the soul and when they are closed as they are here the soul is inaccessible which is a real shame as this would definitely give your shot more impact. Whilst your focus is good on the closed eye the DOF is perhaps a little too shallow at maximum aperture, something like f4 would have given us a nice crisp line of his head against the snow without defining the background too much. Anyway, lots of potential to come we look forward to more from you soon.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An interesting image that contributes well to the open challenge Welcome to DPC Christopher! As a dog lover your image is bound to appeal to me, however, the timing could be better. Its true what they say, the eyes are the gateway to the soul and when they are closed as they are here the soul is inaccessible which is a real shame as this would definitely give your shot more impact. Whilst your focus is good on the closed eye the DOF is perhaps a little too shallow at maximum aperture, something like f4 would have given us a nice crisp line of his head against the snow without defining the background too much. Anyway, lots of potential to come we look forward to more from you soon.', '2017-03-22 15:51:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(7506113, 1196706, 63218, '<td valign="top">Hello Mary your camellia looks fabulous. Great light. Perfect choices in PP. Good work.</td>', 'Hello Mary your camellia looks fabulous. Great light. Perfect choices in PP. Good work.', '2017-03-22 15:56:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(7506115, 1196939, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that contributes well to the open challenge<br/> <br/>A great image Ronnie. Nice composition placing the bird in the most appropriate position. What makes the image is the lovely dawn rim lighting from the sunset. This is not the easiest of exposures  but you have managed well to control the potential underexposure resulting from the backlighting, there is good detail in the birds face and feathers. You have nailed good focus where it should be on the birds eyes. These lovely birds are quite rare over here in the UK, to see one at all is an event in itself but together with this lovely lighting is most unique, well done.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An interesting image that contributes well to the open challenge A great image Ronnie. Nice composition placing the bird in the most appropriate position. What makes the image is the lovely dawn rim lighting from the sunset. This is not the easiest of exposures  but you have managed well to control the potential underexposure resulting from the backlighting, there is good detail in the birds face and feathers. You have nailed good focus where it should be on the birds eyes. These lovely birds are quite rare over here in the UK, to see one at all is an event in itself but together with this lovely lighting is most unique, well done.', '2017-03-22 16:08:26.000000', NULL, 0),
